<h1>vapors demos</h1>
<p>Open one by adding ?demo= and its name to this page's address.</p>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=hello</div><div>F2c S1: a styled panel with text</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=counter</div><div>F2c S2: a button that counts clicks and taps</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=boxes</div><div>F2c S3: borders, rounded corners, shadows, buttons</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=shell</div><div>F2c S4: touche's shell, a grid that drops its panel on a phone</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=panel</div><div>F2c S5: nested components, each with its own scoped CSS</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=text</div><div>F2c S6: a paragraph of bold, italic and code, and a word you can tap</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=stress</div><div>F2c S7: 1,000 elements, a counter ticking every frame, and how long each update takes</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=toasts</div><div>F2c S8: toasts raised above the shell, each kept until dismissed</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=scroll</div><div>F2c S9: two long lists, each scrolling in its own region by wheel and finger</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=images</div><div>F2c S10: a history list with a thumbnail per turn</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=cards</div><div>1-R1: cards whose contents their parent passes as children</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=slider</div><div>3-E3a: a range input bound to a signal, dragged and stepped by key</div></div>
<div class="demo"><div class="name">?demo=image</div><div>F0: the image view, pinch and drag</div></div>
